message: >-
  If you use this software, reference an implementation detail from it, or
  build on its cross-platform parity model, please cite it using the metadata
  below.
title: "2048, built three ways: a parity-tested web, iOS, and Android puzzle"
abstract: >-
  A production-quality implementation of the 2048 sliding-tile puzzle shipped as
  three independent native clients — a dependency-free progressive web app, a
  SwiftUI iOS app, and a Jetpack Compose Android app — that share no runtime code
  yet are held to a single documented set of behavioral invariants. The project
  is a worked example of cross-platform behavioral parity without a shared
  runtime: each client owns its own deterministic rules engine, local-only
  persistence with defensive state validation, injectable randomness for
  reproducible tests, and an accessibility contract covering keyboard, touch,
  screen-reader, reduced-motion, and contrast requirements. Parity is enforced by
  a four-job continuous integration pipeline spanning Node, Xcode, and Gradle
  toolchains.
